module almd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Middle District's own criminal periods. A defendant claiming
// entrapment serves and files written notice within the time for pretrial
// motions, or later as the Court directs; without it entrapment may not be
// raised (LCrR 12(b).1): the period is the court's FRCrimP 12(c) deadline,
// set in each case, so no period is declared. The standard discovery
// procedure is the sole means of criminal discovery except in
// extraordinary circumstances (LCrR 16.1): at arraignment, or on a date
// the court sets for good cause, the government tenders its FRCrimP 16(a),
// Brady and Giglio material, informants' convictions, identification
// procedures, vehicle inspection, latent prints, Rule 404(b) notice and
// surveillance information, and its sentencing information to U.S.
// Probation (16.1(a)(1), (3)); the defendant's reciprocal disclosure is due
// on a date the court sets (16.1(a)(4)); a discovery motion needs a
// certified conference (16.1(c)). Presentence and probation records are
// disclosed only under FRCrimP 32 and this rule, and the officer's
// recommendation not before sentencing (LCrR 32.1). Retained counsel files
// a notice of appearance immediately on being retained (LCrR 44.2).
// Collateral may be forfeited in lieu of appearance under the district's
// schedule (LCrR 58.1). The earlier outline's FRCrimP flow and its
// decisions belong to lit/frcrimp and are removed here: no reporter text
// is vendored.
/// The date set for a revocation hearing at which the defendant will
/// challenge a drug test or its report (M.D. Ala. LCrR 57.1).
event RevocationHearingScheduled()

/// M.D. Ala. LCrR 57.1(1): a defendant challenging a drug test or report
/// in a revocation proceeding notifies the court in writing, with service
/// on the government, fourteen days before the hearing; a late notice
/// needs a motion for leave (57.1(3)).
deadline drug-test-challenge-notice-period: 14.days before RevocationHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "M.D. Ala. LCrR 57.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// M.D. Ala. LCrR 57.1(2): after such a notice, the government files and
/// serves, at least seven days before the hearing "computed in accordance
/// with Fed. R. Crim. P. 45", each laboratory report, the chain-of-custody
/// report and a laboratory employee's affidavit.
deadline drug-test-materials-period: 7.days before RevocationHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "M.D. Ala. LCrR 57.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
